WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
The most informative ablation concerns label propagation.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.600
Applying it on top of a graph neural network
sharply lowers over-robustness.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.440
For instance,

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.280
a GCN combined with label propagation at K equal to
zero-point-five drops its over-robustness

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.120
to about twenty-one percent,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.960
and label propagation on its own achieves the
lowest over-robustness of any method.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.800
Crucially,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.640
this comes for free: adding label propagation does
not hurt test accuracy and often improves

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.480
genuine adversarial robustness while structure
still matters.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.320
The effect is robust to stronger attacks too,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.160
though some over-robustness always remains,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.000
such as eleven-point-four percent for a GCN under
Nettack and nineteen-point-two percent for an MLP.
